From: Lwb89dev <84742481+Lwb89dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: sound: qcom,lpass-tx-macro: allow SM7325 with
 SM8450 fallback

The Motorola Edge 30 (dubai) and the Fairphone 5 (QCM6490) both describe
their TX macro with

	compatible = "qcom,sm7325-lpass-tx-macro", "qcom,sm8450-lpass-tx-macro";

which matches neither branch of the binding: the first branch only
accepts a single compatible, and the second branch pairs the new SoCs
with a constant "qcom,sm8550-lpass-tx-macro" fallback. Add SM7325 to the
paired enum and relax the fallback to the SM8450/SM8550 set both in-tree
users need, so `make CHECK_DTBS` stops reporting these boards.

No functional change; the fallback compatible is the one the driver
matches today.

Reference: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-arm-msm/20260526-sc7280-tx-macro-v1-0-1aad6900fec0@fairphone.com/
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,lpass-tx-macro.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,lpass-tx-macro.yaml
index d8682ff2e..728a3d72e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,lpass-tx-macro.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,lpass-tx-macro.yaml
@@ -23,10 +23,13 @@ properties:
           - enum:
               - qcom,eliza-lpass-tx-macro
               - qcom,kaanapali-lpass-tx-macro
+              - qcom,sm7325-lpass-tx-macro
               - qcom,sm8650-lpass-tx-macro
               - qcom,sm8750-lpass-tx-macro
               - qcom,x1e80100-lpass-tx-macro
-          - const: qcom,sm8550-lpass-tx-macro
+          - enum:
+              - qcom,sm8450-lpass-tx-macro
+              - qcom,sm8550-lpass-tx-macro
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
